---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const title = 'Support — Culprit';
const description =
  'Get help with Culprit. Contact support@getculprit.app, and learn how to delete your account and all of its data.';
---

<Page title={title} heading="Support" description={description}>
  <p>
    Culprit helps pet owners track the foods, symptoms, and moments that shape
    how their pet feels, and turn them into a report their vet can use. If you
    need a hand, we&rsquo;re glad to help.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@getculprit.app">support@getculprit.app</a> and
    a real person will get back to you. Tell us what&rsquo;s happening and, if
    it helps, the device you&rsquo;re on — it lets us sort things out faster.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account and all of its data at any time from within the
    app, in Settings. The deletion removes your pets, your logs, and your
    profile.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prefer we handle it for you? Email
    <a href="mailto:support@getculprit.app">support@getculprit.app</a> from the
    address on your account and we&rsquo;ll take care of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h3>Does Culprit diagnose my pet?</h3>
  <p>
    No. Culprit is a tracking tool. It helps you notice patterns and share them
    with your vet — it doesn&rsquo;t diagnose, treat, or replace veterinary
    care. If you&rsquo;re worried about your pet, your vet is the best call.
  </p>

  <h3>What does it cost?</h3>
  <p>
    The core is free: logging, health flags, trends, and the vet report. There
    is no trial countdown and no per-pet fee.
  </p>

  <h3>How do I get help before launch?</h3>
  <p>
    Culprit is on its way to the App Store. Until then, email
    <a href="mailto:support@getculprit.app">support@getculprit.app</a> with any
    question and we&rsquo;ll reply.
  </p>
</Page>
